  "parsing_notes": "Age range (6-18 years) split into two separate numeric rules (I1, I2); sex field added from CT.gov structured eligibility (ALL) even though not explicitly stated in free text. Labs expressed relative to ULN (INR, ALT, bilirubin) were left unstructured since no absolute cutoff is given. Blood count criteria (hemoglobin, platelets, neutrophils) under a shared 7-day time window were split into three atomic rules sharing time_window_days=7. Medication washout criteria with two different windows (2 months vs 6 months for different drug lists) were split accordingly. Exclusion criteria combining multiple distinct disease entities joined by 'or' (e.g., secondary nephrotic syndrome/SRNS; autoimmune disease/immunodeficiency/malignancy; infection list; vaccine/surgery) were split into separate atomic rules for clearer matching, while true single-condition 'or' statements (e.g., FRNS or SDNS, urine protein criteria, HBsAg/HBcAb combined condition) were kept as one rule since they represent a single overall qualifying/disqualifying state described with internal alternatives. No cohort-specific eligibility differences were found; the age-stratified recruitment groups (≥6-<12 and ≥12-<18) are a recruitment/staging strategy, not distinct eligibility cohorts, so cohorts list is empty."
